+## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)
+
+### Does Amazon S3 support strong consistency for all operations?
+
+Yes, Amazon S3 provides strong read-after-write consistency for PUT, DELETE, and LIST operations of objects in all AWS regions. This applies to both new objects and overwrites of existing objects.
+
+### Can an Amazon RDS Multi-AZ standby instance serve read traffic?
+
+Standard Multi-AZ standby instances are passive and cannot accept read traffic. To scale read volume, you must deploy read replicas or use a Multi-AZ DB cluster deployment with readable standbys.
+
+### Why does a security group not require outbound rules to allow return traffic?
+
+Security groups are stateful firewalls. They automatically track connection states and allow return traffic for any permitted inbound request, regardless of outbound rules.
+
+### How does the Amazon SQS visibility timeout prevent duplicate message processing?
+
+The visibility timeout temporarily hides a message from other consumers while one consumer processes it. If the consumer fails to delete the message before the timeout expires, the message becomes visible again.
