+## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)
+
+### What are the prerequisites for taking the Certified Kubernetes Security Specialist (CKS) exam?
+
+Candidates must hold a currently valid Certified Kubernetes Administrator (CKA) certification to register for the CKS exam. The CKS is a hands-on, performance-based exam that tests practical security skills in a live Kubernetes environment.
+
+### What are the experience requirements to earn the Certified Cloud Security Professional (CCSP) certification?
+
+Candidates need five years of cumulative, paid, full-time IT work experience, including three years in information security and one year in one of the six CCSP domains. An active CISSP credential waives this entire experience requirement, while a relevant degree or the CCSK certificate can waive one year.
+
+### How do you earn the Microsoft Certified: Cybersecurity Architect Expert credential using the SC-100 exam?
+
+To earn this expert-level credential, you must pass the SC-100 exam and hold at least one prerequisite associate certification. Eligible prerequisites include the Azure Security Engineer Associate (AZ-500), Identity and Access Administrator Associate (SC-300), or Security Operations Analyst Associate (SC-200).
+
+### What is the structure and cost of the AWS Certified Security - Specialty (SCS-C02) exam?
+
+The SCS-C02 exam costs 300 USD and consists of 65 multiple-choice or multiple-response questions. Candidates have 170 minutes to complete the exam, which measures skills across six security domains.
