+## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)
+
+### What is the difference between AppSec and DevSecOps?
+
+AppSec focuses on finding and fixing vulnerabilities in application code through manual reviews, threat modeling, and testing. DevSecOps focuses on automating these security checks by building and maintaining scanners directly within the CI/CD pipeline.
+
+### Do I need a software development background to work in DevSecOps?
+
+No, a software development background is not strictly required, though you must understand CI/CD pipelines and automation. Many DevSecOps engineers transition from DevOps, site reliability engineering, or systems administration roles.
+
+### Why does the guide recommend the HashiCorp Terraform Associate certification for cloud security?
+
+Terraform is the industry standard for defining infrastructure as code, including security controls like IAM policies and network boundaries. Validating your Terraform skills proves you can implement security configurations programmatically rather than just auditing them manually.
+
+### How does the Microsoft SC-500 certification differ from older Azure security credentials?
+
+The SC-500 Cloud and AI Security Engineer Associate certification replaces older credentials like AZ-500. It validates your ability to secure traditional Azure cloud infrastructure alongside modern AI workloads, models, and data platforms.
