+## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)
+
+### Why is watching long YouTube tutorials ineffective for learning IT?
+
+Passive watching creates an illusion of competence without building practical skills. Binge-watching multi-hour videos leads to low retention because the brain only recognizes surface-level patterns.
+
+### How can I use YouTube effectively for technical learning?
+
+Use YouTube as a reference tool for high-level introductions, visual concepts, and targeted troubleshooting. Watch videos in 10-to-20-minute chunks, then immediately build the infrastructure in a hands-on environment.
+
+### How do I test my understanding after watching a video?
+
+Recreate the tutorial in your cloud account without rewinding the video. Then, use ExamOS practice modes like Rookie or Challenger to validate your knowledge and identify gaps.
+
+### What is the best way to retain technical information long-term?
+
+Combine short video segments with immediate hands-on building and active recall. Explaining the concept out loud using the Feynman Technique helps solidify your understanding.
